#, no-wrap
msgid "bretonnia/bretonnia.webp"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bretonnian army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$bretonnia.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "Feudal Society"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:96
msgid ""
"The Bretonnian army is essentially an army of Knights and it is the Knights’ "
"contribution to the battle that counts – never mind the pot-washers and clod-"
"breakers. To represent this, the Bretonnian army calculates when it must "
"withdraw from the battle in a different way to other armies.  Instead of "
"counting all of its units at the start of the game, count only the number of "
"units of Knights, Grail Knights and Pegasus Knights. Once the army has lost "
"half or more of its units of Knights/Grail Knights/Pegasus Knights it must "
"withdraw."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[peasants,†1]]1. Peasants"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:106
msgid ""
"A unit of Peasants suffers an additional −1 Command penalty when given an "
"order. However, this penalty is waived if the Peasant unit is part of a "
"brigade that includes at least one non-Peasant unit. Peasants cannot use "
"initiative to charge – though they can use initiative to evade as usual. "
"Peasants are able to make supporting charges. When they charge they receive "
"no bonus attack modifier for doing so."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[knights,†2]]2. Knights"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:112
msgid ""
"A Knight unit will always use its initiative to charge an enemy if possible "
"and cannot be given orders instead. They will never use their initiative to "
"evade. Knights are unaffected by enemy that cause terror in combat and they "
"don’t suffer the usual −1 Attack modifier."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[grail-knights,†3]]3. Grail Knights"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:116
msgid ""
"If the unit of Grail Knights is charging against an enemy in the open it "
"receives an additional +1 Attack modifier in the same way as chariots and "
"monsters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[pegasus-knights,†4]]4. Pegasus Knights"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:118
msgid "Pegasus Knights can fly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:119
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[trebuchet,†5]]5. Trebuchet"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:126
msgid ""
"The Bretonnian Trebuchet is one of the mightiest and most excellent stone "
"throwers that are built in the Old World. At first it was designed to help "
"the noble knights with the sometimes coming up and messy sieges that had to "
"be done but later was adjusted to be used in field battles too. As the "
"Trebuchet is so gargantuan, it uses a 40 x 60mm base, with the short edge "
"being the front."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:130
msgid ""
"To represent that the Trebuchet is such a bulky warmachine, which takes time "
"to assemble and disassemble, the Trebuchets can move but cannot shoot in the "
"turn it moved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:135
msgid ""
"If a Trebuchet is driven back more than 10cm by shooting it is destroyed "
"(drive backs of less than 10cm are simply ignored). If it is forced to "
"retreat from combat it is also destroyed like any other artillery. A "
"Trebuchet is not affected by Gerroff!!! spell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:139
msgid ""
"The Trebuchet has a shooting range of 80cm. Fortified units count as "
"defended and defended targets count as in the open.  No armour roll is made "
"when shot at by a Trebuchet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:141
msgid "The Trebuchet may not shoot at charging enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:145
msgid ""
"The Trebuchet can shoot at targets that it can see as for all other "
"artillery, and it can shoot over the heads of friends and obstacles on lower "
"ground just as can other artillery."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:150
msgid ""
"Shooting Blind: If there is no target in sight a Trebuchet may instead shoot "
"at the nearest enemy unit in range it cannot see.  When Shooting Blind it "
"always hits on 6+ no matter if the target is in the open, defended or even "
"fortified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:151
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[unicorn,†6]]6. Unicorn"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:156
msgid ""
"Only an Enchantress can ride a Unicorn. The Unicorn adds +1 to the "
"Enchantress’s Attacks. Once per battle the Unicorn’s magical power adds +1 "
"to the dice roll when casting a spell. The player must announce that he is "
"using the Unicorn’s magic before rolling to see if the spell works."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[pegasus,†7]]7. Pegasus"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:160
msgid ""
"The Pegasus can be ridden by a General, Hero or Enchantress and adds +1 "
"Attack to the rider as well as allowing the character to fly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:161
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[hippogriff,†8]]8. Hippogriff"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:164
msgid ""
"Only a General can ride a Hippogriff. The Hippogriff can fly. A unit joined "
"by the General on Hippogriff causes terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:165
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[grail-reliquae,†9]]9. Grail Reliquae"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:176
msgid ""
"This sacred item can be given to one unit of Peasants only in a whole army. "
"This unit and all Peasant units touching it become Grail Pilgrims (for as "
"long as they keep contact). Grail Pilgrims are immune to terror, don’t get "
"the −1 Command penalty and get +1 Attack (they still keep the restriction "
"that they don’t get +1 Attacks for charging in the open), they have to "
"attack by initiative if possible and cannot be driven back or confused. "
"Before taking any specific action with a Peasant unit check if they are "
"still touching the unit carrying the Grail Reliquae. If they do so they "
"count as Grail Pilgrims – if not they are simple Peasants."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:177
#, no-wrap
msgid "bretonnia/green-knight.webp"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:179
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bretonnian spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:181
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shield of Combat"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:184
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos.adoc:125
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos-dwarfs.adoc:190
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:185
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:180
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:161
msgid "[.cost]#4+ to cast# [.points]#Range N/A#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:187
msgid ""
"_The enemy’s blows are magically deflected by unseen forces and cause no "
"harm._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:191
msgid ""
"An Enchantress can cast this spell upon a unit that she has joined. The "
"spell lasts until the end of the opposing player’s following turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:196
msgid ""
"The unit can re-roll any failed armour rolls during the Combat phase. This "
"does not include hits suffered from enemy missile fire during a charge, as "
"these are deemed to be shooting hits and are encompassed by the Aerial "
"Shield spell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:200
msgid ""
"Note that only a single re-roll is permitted regardless of what other "
"factors apply. It is never permitted to re-roll a re-roll in any "
"circumstances."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:201
#, no-wrap
msgid "Eerie Mist"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:207
msgid ""
"_An eerie mist rises about the enemy unit stifling the sights and sounds of "
"battle._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:211
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on any enemy unit within range regardless of whether "
"the Enchantress can see it or not. The spell lasts until the end of the "
"opposing player’s following turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:215
msgid ""
"The unit cannot use its initiative. Any order given to the unit, or to any "
"brigade of which it is a part, suffers a −1 Command penalty."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:216
#, no-wrap
msgid "Aerial Shield"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:222
msgid ""
"_The enemy’s missiles sparkle in the sunlight and vanish magically in mid-"
"air causing no harm to their target._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:225
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on a friendly unit whether the Enchantress can see it "
"or not."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:228
msgid ""
"The spell lasts until the beginning of the next Bretonnian Shooting phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:233
msgid ""
"All enemies that shoot at the enchanted unit get −1 on shooting rolls. But "
"keep in mind that regardless of all other circumstances the shooting may "
"never get worse than 6+. So even if the enchanted unit is fortified all "
"enemies still hit on 6+."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:234
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lady’s Favour"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:240
msgid ""
"_A vision of The Lady appears to lead the Bretonnians into the midst of "
"battle or away from danger._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:245
msgid ""
"The spell can be cast on any unengaged friendly unit within range regardless "
"of whether the Enchantress can see it or not.  The spell affects only a "
"single unit, never a brigade and there is no supporting charge possible.."
